issues.body:
Fixes: #296

Blade view-variable typing knows `view('name', [...])` render sites, Livewire `render()`, and Volt — but Filament pages and widgets declare their view as a string property and never call `view()`:

```php
class SettingsPage extends Page {
    public ?TemporaryUploadedFile $uploadedFile = null;
    protected string $view = 'filament.pages.settings';
}
```

So in the template every `$property` is untypable: no hover, no member completion, and the "Cannot resolve type" hint fires on all of them. Given Filament's popularity this hits a lot of real projects.

**Proposed design:** treat a class with a string property named `view` and a **literal** initializer as a render site of that view; feed its typed public properties, `#[Computed]` methods, and `mount()` assignments into the view-variable index under the same precedence rules as the Volt surface (the traversal can be shared rather than duplicated). Non-literal `$view` values are skipped, never guessed. Because such views are often namespaced (`ns::pages.settings`), Blade files also need to map to their namespaced view name — which additionally connects controller `view('ns::…')` render sites to package templates.

Working implementation with 10 tests (one mirrors a real Filament page with `#[Validate]`/`#[Locked]` attribute noise): [`feat/view-property-render-sites`](https://github.com/BastenIT/zed-laravel/tree/feat/view-property-render-sites). Both extraction paths (render-plan capture + direct walker) are hooked, and the plan carries the class surface in an additive serde-defaulted field (cache schema bumps included). Happy to adjust the approach.

Following up on #286 (thanks for the quick merge and the workspace-fence rework!): the root fix makes modular monoliths *usable*, but the module resources themselves are still invisible to the static scans.

The layout (composer-merge-plugin, fairly common for larger Laravel apps):

```
app/{Parent}/{Module}/
├── composer.json          ← merged into the workspace manifest ("extra.laravel.providers" registers the module provider)
├── config/{name}.php      ← merged at boot into config under the "{name}" key (array_replace_recursive)
├── app/Providers/…        ← loadViewsFrom / loadTranslationsFrom / Blade::directive / Livewire::addNamespace
├── resources/views/, lang/
```

What breaks today:

- `config('module-key.…')` → "Config not found" (only the workspace `config/` dir is scanned) — no completion, hover, goto.
- Module providers are never registered (the app scan is `app/Providers` only), so their `loadViewsFrom`/`loadTranslationsFrom` namespaces don't exist → false "View file not found"/"Translation not found" for `ns::…` keys.
- `Livewire::addNamespace(...)` isn't parsed at all (and it's typically called with PHP named arguments, which none of the extractors handle), so `<livewire:ns::component>` errors.

**Proposed design** — an opt-in setting, default off (zero behavior change unless configured):

```jsonc
{
    "lsp": {
        "laravel-lsp": {
            "settings": {
                "modules": {
                    "paths": ["app/Common/*", "app/*/*"]
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

When set: module `config/*.php` merge into their group across all surfaces (via one shared `config_group_files` helper — completion/hover/goto/diagnostics/references/rename/lens); module `*ServiceProvider.php` register like app providers; a tree-sitter extractor handles `Livewire::addNamespace` (positional + named args) plus configurable wrapper methods.

I have a working, fully tested implementation (branch [`feat/modular-monolith-modules`](https://github.com/BastenIT/zed-laravel/tree/feat/modular-monolith-modules), ~1,100 lines incl. tests) that I'm happy to adapt to whatever shape you'd prefer — e.g. different setting names, auto-detection via composer-merge-plugin globs instead of explicit paths, or splitting config/providers/Livewire into separate PRs.
